{"type":"message","id":"65b6b58d","parentId":"ec9a01a6","timestamp":"2026-10-31T18:04:45.079Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Design three distinct fusion sequences. Structure: expose selective with tree branching on producerElements (small producerElements = per-observation reductions ~ tiny; large = matrix-ish? Actually big savings fusedWork << originalWork for producerElements large). The known staged program: expose aggregate threshold 1.02 but consumer_tree threshold 2 (accept most consumers). Mechanism: selective exposure lets 4 matrix cases use tiled schedules. Vary: relax expose threshold (e.g., 1.5) with producerElements branching, vary cleanup threshold (e.g., 1.2, 1.0, 1.05), maybe region-kind policies.\n\nThree proposals:\n\n1. variant-a: expose selective with tree: if producerElements ge 1024 then aggregate accept (threshold 1.02) else threshold 1.0 (reject small tiny gains? no—those gain little). Actually mechanism: unconditional exposure regressed row-scheduled cases; selective exposure via consumer tree threshold 2 allowed tiled. Let's just vary thresholds: expose tree {if producerElements ge 50000 then 1.5 else 1.02}? Hmm — work growth >1 means accepting work growth. Cases with fusedWork ≈ originalWork (row-scheduled) regressed when exposed; but cleanup recovered them. Four improved cases had big reductions (fusedWork ~half original).\n\nProposal 1: expose threshold relaxed to 1.5 via aggregate threshold (accept cases where fused <= 1.5*original — this includes the ~equal ones, which regressed but cleanup recovers). cleanup threshold 1.02 (default). This widens exposure to allow tiled schedules for marginal cases.\n\nProposal 2: expose tree on producerElements: large producers (ge 100000, matrix-like) get 2.0; small (lt 100000) get 1.02. cleanup threshold 1.05.\n\nProposal 3: region-kind? Region selector for expose? Expose policy must be one of policy kinds; region kind allowed as a policy? \"one kind\" — region is a kind. Try expose region {max_work_growth 1.5, launch_work moderate, materialization_work small}, cleanup threshold 1.02. Keep trees simple; node limit 31.\n\nWrite JSONs.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The traces show two regimes: cases with large savings (fusedWork ≈ half of originalWork, matrix-like producers with large `producerElements`) and near-neutral cases (fusedWork ≈ originalWork, small producers). The staged winner's mechanism suggests exposure unlocks tiled schedules for the big-win cases, while near-neutral exposures regress but cleanup recovers them. I'll probe three structural hypotheses: (a) wider expose growth allowed universally with default cleanup, (b) size-gated exposure, (c) region-based exposure jointly modeling launch/materialization costs."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d1b444ae49254af9b24640b9","name":"submit_policy","arguments":{"policy_json":"{\"format\":\"kiln-transformation-program/1\",\"id\":\"wide-expose-a\",\"kind\":\"fusion-sequence\",\"expose\":{\"format\":\"kiln-fusion-policy/1\",\"id\":\"expose-wide-a\",\"kind\":\"threshold\",\"max_work_growth\":1.5},\"cleanup\":{\"format\":\"kiln-fusion-policy/1\",\"id\":\"cleanup-a\",\"kind\":\"threshold\",\"max_work_growth\":1.02}}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_a0ee2a30c2774073b8d9b10b","name":"submit_policy","arguments":{"policy_json":"{\"format\":\"kiln-transformation-program/1\",\"id\":\"size-gated-b\",\"kind\":\"fusion-sequence\",\"expose\":{\"format\":\"kiln-fusion-policy/1\",\"id\":\"expose-gated-b\",\"kind\":\"selective\",\"tree\":{\"if\":{\"feature\":\"producerElements\",\"op\":\"ge\",\"value\":100000},\"then\":{\"threshold\":2},\"else\":{\"threshold\":1.02}},\"consumer_tree\":{\"threshold\":2}},\"cleanup\":{\"format\":\"kiln-fusion-policy/1\",\"id\":\"cleanup-b\",\"kind\":\"threshold\",\"max_work_growth\":1.05}}"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_285aee26f54f4a88bc760bd0","name":"submit_policy","arguments":{"policy_json":"{\"format\":\"kiln